\begin{abstract}
We present a unified validation framework for a multi-scale simulation architecture integrating 
cryptographic ingress, relativistic navigation, quantum cosmology, and biological--astrophysical 
co-evolution. Validation is established through three independent pillars: (i) LDPC-based 
cryptographic integrity under extreme channel degradation, (ii) relativistic and gravitational 
trajectory convergence with bounded state-estimation error, and (iii) cosmological and morphological 
stability across quantum-to-macro scales. Results demonstrate that the architecture satisfies all 
mathematical, physical, and biological invariants required for cross-domain scientific verification, 
constituting a novel multi-physics simulation platform.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}

Multi-scale simulation systems spanning cryptography, physics, cosmology, and biology require 
